---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Phone from '../components/Phone.astro';
import Contours from '../components/Contours.astro';
import { site, appLink, appLinkLabel, isBeta } from '../data/site';
import '../styles/home.css';
---
<SiteLayout>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-grid wrap">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>You’re being<br /><em>watched.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-intro">There are cameras all along your drive.<br class="desktop-break" /> You’re Flocked helps you see them coming.</p>
        <p class="hero-description">See nearby cameras, get a heads-up as you approach, and find a route past fewer of them. Right on your iPhone.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#get-flckd">Join the beta <Icon name="arrow" /></a><a class="text-link" href="#the-app">Take a look <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
        <div class="hero-note"><Icon name="check" /><span>No accounts. No tracking. Open source.</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-visual">
        <Contours />
        <div class="map-orbit" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <Phone image="routing" alt="The You’re Flocked route planner showing a teal route around nearby cameras." class="hero-route" eager />
        <Phone image="camera-map" alt="The You’re Flocked camera map showing community-mapped cameras around Oklahoma City." class="hero-map" eager />
        <div class="map-note"><span class="note-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>You’re Flocked. Now you know.</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="intro-section wrap" id="the-app">
    <h2>A better picture of<br />the road around you.</h2>
    <p>License plate readers. Speed cameras. The camera you’ve driven past a hundred times without noticing. You’re Flocked puts them on the map, using locations contributed by people who spotted them.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-section wrap" aria-labelledby="map-heading">
    <div class="feature-art map-art"><Phone image="camera-map" alt="A map filled with red camera markers and their recorded viewing directions." /><span class="art-caption">The camera map. Every dot is a camera someone spotted and mapped.</span></div>
    <div class="feature-copy">
      <h2 id="map-heading">A heads-up.<br />Not a guessing game.</h2>
      <p>Open the map to see what’s nearby. The app shows automated license plate readers (ALPR), speed cameras, and other surveillance equipment, with viewing directions where the data is available.</p>
      <p>You don’t have to keep staring at the screen, either. Proximity alerts let you know when you’re getting close, even with your phone in your pocket.</p>
      <ul class="check-list"><li><Icon name="check" />Community-mapped camera locations</li><li><Icon name="check" />Alerts at a distance you choose</li><li><Icon name="check" />Filters for the cameras you care about</li></ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-section reverse wrap" aria-labelledby="route-heading">
    <div class="feature-art route-art"><Phone image="routing" alt="An example route with an avoidance slider, travel time, distance and camera count." /><span class="art-caption">The route planner, steering around all 71 cameras nearby.</span></div>
    <div class="feature-copy">
      <h2 id="route-heading">Same destination.<br /><em>Fewer cameras.</em></h2>
      <p>Pick where you’re going and how much you’d like to avoid cameras. You’re Flocked weighs the options and plans a route, entirely on your phone.</p>
      <p>Download a region pack before you head out. The routing engine works from that saved road data, so planning a route doesn’t need a round trip to a server.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href={site.tiles} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Browse routing regions <Icon name="external" /></a>
      <p class="fine-print">Routes use known camera locations. They can reduce exposure, not guarantee a camera-free drive.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="privacy-section">
    <div class="privacy-grid wrap">
      <div class="privacy-heading"><Icon name="shield" /><h2>Your phone should<br />look out for you.<br /><em>Not keep tabs on you.</em></h2></div>
      <div class="privacy-copy"><p>Telling you there’s a camera up ahead doesn’t take an account, a record of your trips, or a pile of analytics. So the app doesn’t ask for any of them.</p><p>You’re Flocked calculates proximity alerts and routes on your device. There’s no location history, no telemetry, and no routing server receiving your start point and destination.</p><p class="privacy-caveat">That doesn’t make the whole app offline. Camera lookups use DeFlock and OpenStreetMap, and map imagery comes from Apple. The privacy page spells out what those services receive.</p><a class="text-link" href="/privacy/">Read what leaves your phone <Icon /></a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="community-section wrap">
    <div><h2>Open source.<br />In good company.</h2><p>You’re Flocked is inspired by DeFlock and built on camera data people contribute to OpenStreetMap. It’s a small part of a much bigger effort to make surveillance visible.</p><a class="text-link" href={site.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Have a look under the hood <Icon name="github" /></a></div>
    <div class="community-links"><a href="https://deflock.me" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span><strong>DeFlock</strong><small>Meet the project that inspired this one.</small></span><Icon name="external" /></a><a href="/hosting/"><span><strong>Host the road data yourself.</strong><small>Run your own copy of the routing-data server.</small></span><Icon /></a><a href="/press/"><span><strong>Writing about You’re Flocked?</strong><small>Screenshots, the short version, and the details.</small></span><Icon /></a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq-section wrap" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <h2 id="faq-heading">A few things<br />worth knowing.</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details><summary>Does it know about every camera?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. Camera locations are contributed by people, so coverage depends on what’s been mapped in your area. Missing or outdated locations are possible. You’re Flocked is an awareness tool, not a guarantee that you won’t be recorded.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can I use it without an internet connection?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Route calculation works offline once you’ve downloaded the right region pack. Alerts keep working from camera data already on your phone. Fresh camera lookups, place searches, and Apple map imagery still need a connection.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What phones does it work on?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>The current app is an iPhone beta, installed through TestFlight, and needs iOS 17 or later. Android is planned, but isn’t available yet.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do I need to run a server?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. Out of the box, the app downloads its road data from tiles.flckd.app. Self-hosting is for people who’d rather serve that data from their own machine. Either way, routes are calculated on your phone. <a href="/hosting/">Read the self-hosting guide.</a></p></details>
      <details><summary>Is it FLCKD or You’re Flocked?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Both. The app is called You’re Flocked. FLCKD is the short name that fits under the icon on your home screen, so that’s what you’ll see on your phone.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Is this affiliated with Flock Safety?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. You’re Flocked is an independent project. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Flock Safety.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="get-section" id="get-flckd"><div class="wrap get-inner"><img src="/images/app-icon.webp" alt="The You’re Flocked app icon" width="80" height="80" /><h2>Go your own way.<br /><em>A little more informed.</em></h2><p>You’re Flocked for iPhone is in public beta. Install it through TestFlight.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={appLink} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{appLinkLabel}<Icon name="external" /></a><a class="button secondary" href={site.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener"><Icon name="github" /> View on GitHub</a></div>{isBeta && <p class="fine-print">It’s a beta, so expect rough edges and the occasional change between builds. You’ll need Apple’s free TestFlight app and iOS 17 or later.<br />Prefer to build it yourself? <a href={site.build} target="_blank" rel="noopener">The source and instructions are on GitHub.</a></p>}</div></section>
</SiteLayout>
